<title>MEXICO: FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 22.09 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 22.09 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 93 basis points to 22.09 percent, and rates are seen mixed at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY	CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     21.16	    22.09		   + 93 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     22.81	    22.95		   + 14 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    23.33	    23.41		   +  8 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     24.49	    24.43		   -  6 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST/2330 GMT.</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
</text>
